// builtins.memql -- workbench namespace
//
// Builtins bridge MemQL tool calls to the Go integration handlers.
// The tool surface in the product pack's tools file references
// @handler(type="function", name="workbenchDispatchHost"); that
// name resolves to this builtin, which forwards to the workbench
// integration's `dispatchHost` capability.

// `environment` is the OPTIONAL HINT (memql#4353, design 6.1):
// { os: "<goos>", needs: ["display"|"gpu"|"macos_tooling"|"user_files"] }.
// The agent says what the action needs; handleDispatchHost compares it with
// what a workbench IS -- Linux, headless, no user files -- and returns a typed
// `environment_mismatch` NAMING THE UNMET NEEDS instead of running the action
// and failing obscurely three layers down (a `defaults read` on Linux, an
// xdotool with no DISPLAY, a path under /Users that is not there).
//
// A mismatch is not a failure and not a switch. The tool loop reroutes to the
// user's own fleet ONLY when the plan already holds standing scope at the level
// the needs imply and the task is approved; otherwise it raises the consent
// card exactly as the knowledge corpus prescribes. The corpus's prohibition on
// silent switching stands, and is quoted in the Go that implements this.
//
// Omitted entirely means "no hint" -- every pre-#4353 caller, and every action
// that genuinely does not care. There is no default hint; guessing one would
// make the mismatch fire on calls that would have worked.
@executor("integration.workbench.dispatchHost")
@args(profile="object")
@description("Dispatch a workbenchHost.<action> call to the per-Plan workbench workspace. Lazily provisions the workspace on first call; subsequent calls in the same Plan see persisted files.")
builtin workbenchDispatchHost {
  action       string!
  args         object
  planId       string
  agentId      string
  taskId       string
  environment  object
}

// workbenchTeardownDirectory -- on-disk teardown of a per-Plan
// workspace. Called from the releaseWorkspaceOnPlanTerminal logic
// alongside releaseWorkspace (which flips the lifecycle
// bit on the concept row). The integration removes the directory
// tree under MEMQL_WORKBENCH_ROOT/{planId}/. Idempotent: a Plan
// that never provisioned a workspace is a no-op.

@executor("integration.workbench.teardownDirectory")
@args(profile="object")
@description("Remove the on-disk workbench workspace directory for a Plan. Idempotent. Called by the releaseWorkspaceOnPlanTerminal automation after the concept row has been flipped to released.")
builtin workbenchTeardownDirectory {
  planId  string!
}
